<section id="Pt0.A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">0.A.2 </span>Dataset</h3>

<div id="Pt0.A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A detailed pipeline in creating the indirect connections and its relevant test set samples are provided in the Figure <a href="#Pt0.A1.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 0.A.2 Dataset ‣ Indirect Connection generation ‣ Q&amp;A Generation ‣ 0.A.1 Prompts ‣ Appendix 0.A Appendix ‣ Standard vs. Modular Sampling: Best Practices for Reliable LLM Unlearning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. First, we use the prompt <a href="#Pt0.A1.SS1.SSSx2" title="Indirect Connection generation ‣ Q&amp;A Generation ‣ 0.A.1 Prompts ‣ Appendix 0.A Appendix ‣ Standard vs. Modular Sampling: Best Practices for Reliable LLM Unlearning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">0.A.1</span></a> to generate 6 entities for each target. Followed by we scrape their wiki pages and generate Q&amp;As with the LLaMA 3.3 70B model <a href="#Pt0.A1.SS1.SSSx1" title="Q&amp;A Generation ‣ 0.A.1 Prompts ‣ Appendix 0.A Appendix ‣ Standard vs. Modular Sampling: Best Practices for Reliable LLM Unlearning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">0.A.1</span></a> in an Interrogative syntactic structure manner to maintain the <math id="Pt0.A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\textit{N}_{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">N</mtext><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\textit{N}_{s})</annotation></semantics></math> neighbor dataset.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Pt0.A1.F4" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.05316v1/indirect.png" id="Pt0.A1.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/107;" width="476" height="107" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Pt0.A1.F4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 4</span>: </span><span id="Pt0.A1.F4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Pipeline in creating Indirect connections for retain and test set</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="Pt0.A1.F5" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.05316v1/retain_test_gen.png" id="Pt0.A1.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/119;" width="476" height="119" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Pt0.A1.F5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 5</span>: </span><span id="Pt0.A1.F5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Generation of Test set samples for the Direct Neighbors</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="Pt0.A1.F7" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="Pt0.A1.F7.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_bottom" style="width:165.6pt;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.05316v1/num_forget_retain_samples.svg" id="Pt0.A1.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:229/190;" width="229" height="190"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Pt0.A1.F7.fig1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 6</span>: </span><span id="Pt0.A1.F7.fig1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Composition of Forget-Retain samples per target</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="Pt0.A1.F7.fig2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_bottom" style="width:165.6pt;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.05316v1/direct_n_indirect_num_samples.svg" id="Pt0.A1.F7.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:229/190;" width="229" height="190"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="Pt0.A1.F7.fig2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 7</span>: </span><span id="Pt0.A1.F7.fig2.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Composition of Direct and Indirect retain samples per target</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
</figure>
<section id="Pt0.A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">0.A.3 </span>Experimental setup</h3>

<div id="Pt0.A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model Finetuning</span>: Before the application of unlearning, we initially finetune the model on the all the datasets we have i.e., <math id="Pt0.A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{f},D_{r},D_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{f},D_{r},D_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. We use the questions as prompts and conduct a Supervised Fine-tuning on the datasets. Given <math id="Pt0.A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{ft}=D_{f}+D_{r}+D_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{ft}=D_{f}+D_{r}+D_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, and its samples <math id="Pt0.A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math>, <span id="Pt0.A1.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">x</span> is question and <span id="Pt0.A1.SS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">y</span> is the answer. A pair <math id="Pt0.A1.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}=p(x_{i},y_{i})\in D_{ft}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}=p(x_{i},y_{i})\in D_{ft}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A1.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{1},..y_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{1},..y_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> are the answer tokens, we calculate Negative-Log-Likelihood (NLL) loss for <math id="Pt0.A1.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Pt0.A1.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.E1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}(y\mid x;\theta)=\mathrm{NLL}(y\mid x;\theta)=-\sum_{t=1}^{T}\log p\bigl(y_{t}\mid x,y_{&lt;t};\theta\bigr)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>NLL</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(y\mid x;\theta)=\mathrm{NLL}(y\mid x;\theta)=-\sum_{t=1}^{T}\log p\bigl(y_{t}\mid x,y_{&lt;t};\theta\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Unlearning Methods:</h4>

<section id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"></h5>

<div id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Gradient Ascent (GA)</span>is the most straightforward unlearning technique proposed for the Un-targeted unlearning. It’s main idea is to maximize the loss as opposed to the training objective of minimization by negating the loss. In our work, we do not implement this. Due to its nature of negation, the maximization becomes unbounded leading to catastrophic collapse. The predicted loss <math id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l(y|x;\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l(y|x;\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> on forget set can be written as:</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Pt0.A1.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{GA}(D_{f};\theta)=-\,\mathcal{L}(y_{f}\mid x_{f};\theta)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{GA}(D_{f};\theta)=-\,\mathcal{L}(y_{f}\mid x_{f};\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"></h5>

<div id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Gradient Difference (GD)</span>proposed by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite> to mitigate the issues of Gradient ascent. It builds on the concept of Gradient Ascent, but not only aims to maximize the loss on forget set <math id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>, simultaneously minimizes the loss on the retain set <math id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. This maintains the balance of forgetting and retaining. The loss function can be written as:</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Pt0.A1.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{GD}(\theta)=\mathcal{-L}(D_{f};\theta)+\mathcal{L}(D_{r};\theta)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{GD}(\theta)=\mathcal{-L}(D_{f};\theta)+\mathcal{L}(D_{r};\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"></h5>

<div id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Direct Preference Optimization (DPO)</span>is proposed by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite> and was first used by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>]</cite>, treats unlearning as a preference optimization problem by applying the standard DPO loss. This technique uses <span id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Targeted Unlearning</span>, making a necessity of replacement responses like "I don’t know". Alike the standard DPO approach, we use "I don’t know" responses as positive samples and forget set as negative samples to guide the model’s response. For the implementation of DPO, we convert the forget set to a preference dataset containing winning responses and refusal responses. Preference dataset <math id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{p}={(x_{i},y_{i,win},y_{i,lose})},i\in|D_{f}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{p}={(x_{i},y_{i,win},y_{i,lose})},i\in|D_{f}|</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i,win}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i,win}</annotation></semantics></math> are randomly chosen from a subset of "I don’t know" phrases, and <math id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i,lose}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i,lose}</annotation></semantics></math> are the forget targets.
The DPO loss can be calculated as:</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Pt0.A1.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{DPO,\beta}(\theta)=-\,\mathbb{E}_{D_{p}}\Biggl[\log\sigma\Bigl(\beta\log\frac{p(y_{\mathrm{win}}\mid x;\theta)}{p(y_{\mathrm{win}}\mid x;\theta_{\mathrm{ref}})}\;-\;\beta\log\frac{p(y_{\mathrm{lose}}\mid x;\theta)}{p(y_{\mathrm{lose}}\mid x;\theta_{\mathrm{ref}})}\Bigr)\Biggr]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>win</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>win</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>lose</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>lose</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{DPO,\beta}(\theta)=-\,\mathbb{E}_{D_{p}}\Biggl[\log\sigma\Bigl(\beta\log\frac{p(y_{\mathrm{win}}\mid x;\theta)}{p(y_{\mathrm{win}}\mid x;\theta_{\mathrm{ref}})}\;-\;\beta\log\frac{p(y_{\mathrm{lose}}\mid x;\theta)}{p(y_{\mathrm{lose}}\mid x;\theta_{\mathrm{ref}})}\Bigr)\Biggr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> is the sigmoid function and <math id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> is the inverse temperature controlling the preference strength. We use <math id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=0.1</annotation></semantics></math> for all our experiments. Provided, we have a retain set, we utilize the code implementation provided by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite>, can be calculated as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Pt0.A1.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{DPO+retain}}=\alpha\,\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{DPO},\beta}(\theta)+\gamma\,\mathcal{L}(D_{r};\theta)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>DPO</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>retain</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>DPO</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{DPO+retain}}=\alpha\,\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{DPO},\beta}(\theta)+\gamma\,\mathcal{L}(D_{r};\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Where <math id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> are hyperparameter to control the strength of DPO loss and NLL. For our experiments, both <math id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is always 1.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"></h5>

<div id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Negative Preference Optimization (NPO) -</span> proposed by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">38</a>]</cite>, is an inspiration of DPO, a variant that uses only the negative responses from the <math id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>, disregarding the <math id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{win}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{win}</annotation></semantics></math> making it an Un-targeted Unlearning. For the implementation, we ignore the "I don’t know" responses and provide only <math id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{f},y_{f})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{f},y_{f})</annotation></semantics></math>. Followed by, we calculate retain loss similarly as in DPO + retain with the same hyper-parameters values <math id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\beta,\alpha,\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\beta,\alpha,\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Pt0.A1.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{NPO,\beta}(\theta)=-\frac{2}{\beta}\,\mathbb{E}_{D_{p}}\Biggl[\log\sigma\Bigl(\;-\;\beta\log\frac{p(y_{\mathrm{lose}}\mid x;\theta)}{p(y_{\mathrm{lose}}\mid x;\theta_{\mathrm{ref}})}\Bigr)\Biggr]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>lose</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>lose</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{NPO,\beta}(\theta)=-\frac{2}{\beta}\,\mathbb{E}_{D_{p}}\Biggl[\log\sigma\Bigl(\;-\;\beta\log\frac{p(y_{\mathrm{lose}}\mid x;\theta)}{p(y_{\mathrm{lose}}\mid x;\theta_{\mathrm{ref}})}\Bigr)\Biggr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx1.Px4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Pt0.A1.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{NPO+retain}}=\alpha\,\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{NPO},\beta}(\theta)+\gamma\,\mathcal{L}(D_{r};\theta)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>NPO</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>retain</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>NPO</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{NPO+retain}}=\alpha\,\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{NPO},\beta}(\theta)+\gamma\,\mathcal{L}(D_{r};\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection">Evaluation Metrics:</h4>

<div id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ROUGE (R)</span> quantifies the world-level overlap between the model’s output and the ground-truth answer. We compute the ROUGE-L <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite> score between the generated response <math id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(x;\theta_{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(x;\theta_{*})</annotation></semantics></math> and the ground-truth answer <span id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">y</span>, written as <math id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ROUGE-L(g(x;\theta_{*}),y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ROUGE-L(g(x;\theta_{*}),y)</annotation></semantics></math>. ROUGE-L provides the longest sequence overlap and the verbatim memory of the Unlearned Model <math id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(M;\theta_{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>;</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(M;\theta_{*})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cosine Similarity (CS)</span> measures the semantic similarity of the model’s output against the ground-truth. We follow <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>]</cite> setup, embed both with Sentence-BERT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>]</cite>, calculate the cosine similarity and truncate the values less than 0.</p>
<table id="Pt0.A1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max\bigl(\cos\bigl(g(x;\theta_{*}),\,y\bigr),\,0\bigr)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn> 0</mn><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max\bigl(\cos\bigl(g(x;\theta_{*}),\,y\bigr),\,0\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Probability (P)</span> defines the average likelihood assigned to each token given a question and its ground truth answer i.e., <math id="Pt0.A1.SS3.SSSx2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math>. Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>]</cite>, we compute normalized conditional probability as</p>
<table id="Pt0.A1.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}(y\mid x)=\tfrac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}p\bigl(y_{t}\mid x\circ y_{&lt;t};\,\theta_{*}\bigr)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">;</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}(y\mid x)=\tfrac{1}{T}\sum_{t=1}^{T}p\bigl(y_{t}\mid x\circ y_{&lt;t};\,\theta_{*}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="Pt0.A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">0.A.4 </span>Results</h3>

<figure id="Pt0.A1.T1" class="ltx_table">

<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="Pt0.A1.T1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 1</span>: </span><span id="Pt0.A1.T1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Experimental results.</span></figcaption><div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="Pt0.A1.T1.5" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><span id="Pt0.A1.T1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:70%;">Dataset Practices
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:3.0pt;"><span id="Pt0.A1.T1.5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">

<span id="Pt0.A1.T1.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<span class="ltx_tbody">
<span id="Pt0.A1.T1.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="Pt0.A1.T1.5.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt" style="padding:-0.4pt 5.0pt;">Method</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.T1.5.1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:-0.4pt 5.0pt;">FE <math id="Pt0.A1.T1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.T1.5.1.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:-0.4pt 5.0pt;">MU-T <math id="Pt0.A1.T1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.T1.5.1.1.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:-0.4pt 5.0pt;">PPL-F <math id="Pt0.A1.T1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.T1.5.1.1.1.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:-0.4pt 5.0pt;">PPL-T<math id="Pt0.A1.T1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.T1.5.1.1.1.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding:-0.4pt 5.0pt;">MMLU %</span></span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.T1.5.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="Pt0.A1.T1.5.1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding:-0.4pt 5.0pt;">Pre-Unlearning</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.T1.5.1.1.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:-0.4pt 5.0pt;">0.30</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.T1.5.1.1.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:-0.4pt 5.0pt;">0.73</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.T1.5.1.1.1.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:-0.4pt 5.0pt;">38.76</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.T1.5.1.1.1.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:-0.4pt 5.0pt;">37105</span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.T1.5.1.1.1.2.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding:-0.4pt 5.0pt;">12.42</span></span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.T1.5.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="Pt0.A1.T1.5.1.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t ltx_colspan ltx_colspan_6" style="padding:-0.4pt 5.0pt;"><span id="Pt0.A1.T1.5.1.1.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Gradient-based (Un-Targeted)</span></span></span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.T1.5.1.1.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
